  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LAND-at-scale &#x2013; Egypt - Participatory Land-Use Consolidation for Climate Resilience and Inclusive Business Models</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is being implemented as part of the LAND-at-scale programme, focusing on scaling participatory land-use consolidation to address land fragmentation in Egypt. The main objectives of the project are to 1)	Assess the suitability and applicability of various land-use consolidation tools including the development of inclusive business models; 2)	Raise awareness, mobilize communities, and strengthen capacities at the local, governorate, and national levels; 3)	Pilot land-use consolidation models, focusing on 1)	Crop consolidation and private sector engagement; and 2)	Land-use consolidation tailored for climate adaptation including demonstration plots; and to 3)	Facilitate learning, knowledge dissemination, and policy advocacy in collaboration with the government to enable scaling up of successful practices.</narrative>
  </description>
